tes also asserts sovereignty over five major island territories and various uninhabited islands in Oceania and the Caribbean. It is a megadiverse country, with the world's fourth-largest total area and third-largest population, exceeding 341 million.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States","source":"Wikipedia","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","iso2":"US"},{"title":"Iran","extract":"Iran, officially the Islamic Republic of Iran, and historically known as Persia, is a country in West Asia. It borders Iraq to the west; Turkey, Azerbaijan, and Armenia to the northwest; the Caspian Sea to the north, Turkmenistan to the northeast; Afghanistan to the east; Pakistan to the southeast; and the Gulf of Oman and the Persian Gulf to the south. With a population of over 92 million, Iran ranks 17th globally in both geographic size and population. It is divided into five regions with 31 provinces. Tehran is the nation's capital and largest city and serves as its primary economic center.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iran","source":"Wikipedia","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","iso2":"IR"}],"arc":{"reports":72,"first_seen":"2026-10-11T12:20:00Z","first_title":"US military disables ship attempting to bypass Strait of Hormuz blockade","first_url":"https://news.google.?oc=5","first_publisher":"The Hill","earlier":[{"id":"e_ed1871b061b6","title":"Iran gives 2-day window for Hormuz deal as US mulls strikes: What to know","date":"2026-11-02T20:09:17Z","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiqwFBVV95cUxNUkVuYzVQaks4RzQxUm9oNzJNTmVIQUl4WF9WS0JETVZ1TjFnQ0dkd3dOUjBOQlNqMkxyLUpfTFI1VDE3NC1faXFIZkZpRlRZc0tYOXNab29KbGgzZnpFNXRRQTRPZW5OS2p6Z0VCMGhKcUlMY04yeTRiU3YzM3Bxc01qT1BFeF8zaUw1SGxVX3l3ZTh6eGZTc2J2QVFzTHNRSEk0NV9lODg2Rm8?oc=5","publisher":"Al-Monitor","verification":"single_source_report"},{"id":"e_e13644d3192e","title":"US says, Strait of Hormuz set to open for commercial shipping","date":"2026-11-03T01:07:37Z","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMijwFBVV95cUxQVXdIdTlO